    "reasoning": "**Analyzing SSD1306 Connections**\n\nI\u2019m looking into the pin configurations for the SSD1306. There\u2019s a distinction between VCC, which is for the OLED panel\u2019s power supply, and VBAT, related to the charge pump output. It appears there might be some mismatches in the datasheet, especially with VBAT being described as a high-voltage input. While examining the netlist shows some disconnected pins, it raises questions about whether VCC could actually be an output generated from the charge pump.**Examining SSD1306 Circuit Design**\n\nI\u2019m reviewing the SSD1306 datasheet for the typical circuit configuration. VDD is for logic supply, while VCC is meant for the OLED panel. It's possible that VCC could connect to an external 7.5V power supply or be linked to an internal charge pump. However, I wonder if VBAT is a standard for the SSD1306 or just a custom representation used by the module. There\u2019s a bit of ambiguity here that I want to clarify!"
