              "type": "reasoning.summary",
              "summary": "**Analyzing supply connections**\n\nI\u2019m looking into the input tied to VCC and the internal pump step to VBAT for the panel drive. It seems like pin 28 is designated for logic supply, which is unclear since there\u2019s an isolated pin mentioned. The specifications imply that C7 should connect to the VCC rail, but the connectivity description doesn\u2019t clarify this. It'll help to check that U4's designated VDD pin is the actual VCC. There might be confusion with custom symbols, and I need to clarify this issue.**Examining spec mismatches**\n\nI\u2019m noticing an exact mismatch for the R5 specification and a possible issue with C18 that\u2019s not addressed in the report. It seems like U4 pin 28 may be an anomaly due to contradictions in the schematic. When analyzing the SSD1306 standard, I see pins for VDD, VSS, and VCC. The datasheet indicates that VCC is the power supply for the OLED panel, generated internally. Additionally, there\u2019s some ambiguity around the VBAT pin, which could be nonstandard in this context.**Clarifying SSD1306 pin designations**\n\nI've realized that the actual SSD1306 doesn\u2019t include a VBAT pin, which makes me wonder if it could be related to the OLED panel anode. The standard SSD1306 has 30 pins, including VCC, VDD, VSS, and no mention of VBAT. It\u2019s possible that the symbol labeled \"VBAT\" in the custom module header might actually refer to the panel supply, while the VCC pin could serve as the charge pump output. This is quite the puzzle!",
